    EXCERPT FIXTURE, the no-averaged-section control. Same source and same two
    edits as copper-two-section.edi: the HEAD and DEFINEMEAS blocks and both
    MTSECT sections are cut verbatim from the GSSA Copper Coast MT 2020 open-file
    release (Geological Survey of South Australia, CC-BY-4.0, SARIG document
    record mesac2282), served in the AusMT corpus as
    surveys/copper-coast-2020/transfer_functions/edi/Wp01.edi; this INFO block
    replaces the source's EPI-KIT JSON block, and every data block is truncated
    to its first seven frequencies with NFREQ and the comment counts restated. No
    value is altered.

    The sections kept are XPR-0 and XPR-99, so this file carries NEITHER a
    DATAID_avg section NOR one named for its DATAID. It is the control for the
    last clause of the rule: with no solution of record to name, the FIRST
    section stands. XPR-99 is almost entirely the EMPTY sentinel, which is what
    the last realisation of a 100-estimate stack looks like and what a
    last-section reader would publish.

    No angle bracket appears in this block on purpose: mt_metadata's DEFINEMEAS
    scanner keys on the two-character sequence anywhere in a line, INFO block
    included, and would read this prose as measurement metadata.

